---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
const baseUrl = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<DocsLayout 
  title="System Diagnostics, Health & Telemetry" 
  description="Native OMV diagnostics page, CLI telemetry subcommands, live tmux session monitor, and service log streaming."
  category="Security & Ops"
  prevPage={{ title: "Security & Credential Vault", href: `${baseUrl}/docs/security` }}
  nextPage={{ title: "Architecture & Overview", href: `${baseUrl}/docs` }}
>
  <div class="docs-callout docs-callout-info">
    <strong>📊 Built-In Observability:</strong><br />
    The Agent Station provides real-time health checks, memory benchmarking, and service logs directly within the OpenMediaVault WebGUI as well as via the <code>omv-agent-station</code> CLI utility.
  </div>

  <h2>🖥️ OpenMediaVault WebGUI Diagnostics Page</h2>
  <p>
    Inside the OMV WebGUI, navigate to <strong>Diagnostics ➔ Agent Station</strong>:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Services Status Table:</strong> Real-time container state, uptime, port mappings, and memory consumption for <code>litellm-proxy</code>, <code>telegram-agent-bot</code>, <code>syncthing</code>, and <code>ttyd</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Tmux Sessions Monitor:</strong> Lists all background autonomous agent sessions with CPU usage and running processes.</li>
    <li><strong>Service Logs Streamer:</strong> Choose any service from the dropdown (LiteLLM, Telegram Bot, Signal, Discord, System) to inspect the last 100 log lines with one click.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>⚡ CLI Subcommands (<code>omv-agent-station</code>)</h2>
  <p>
    Manage and inspect the stack from any terminal:
  </p>

  <pre><code># 1. Full system status summary
sudo omv-agent-station status

# 2. Memory & CPU resource benchmark
sudo omv-agent-station performance

# 3. Stream live logs from specific container
sudo omv-agent-station logs telegram-bot
sudo omv-agent-station logs litellm-proxy

# 4. Re-apply WebGUI configuration to .env and restart containers
sudo omv-agent-station apply

# 5. Full stack restart
sudo omv-agent-station restart</code></pre>

  <h2>🩺 Troubleshooting Common Issues</h2>
  <table class="docs-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Symptom</th>
        <th>Likely Cause</th>
        <th>Recommended Solution</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>Unauthorized access</code> in Telegram</td>
        <td><code>TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_USER_ID</code> does not match your numeric ID</td>
        <td>Send <code>/start</code> to <code>@userinfobot</code> in Telegram, copy your ID, and update it in OMV WebGUI ➔ Agent Station ➔ Chat.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>The chat is not a forum</code> error</td>
        <td>Group does not have Topics enabled</td>
        <td>In Telegram Group Settings ➔ <strong>Edit</strong> ➔ Turn ON <strong>Topics</strong> and promote bot to Admin.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>LiteLLM <code>No active route configured</code></td>
        <td>AI provider keys missing in <code>.env</code></td>
        <td>Add your Gemini API Key or GitHub Token in OMV WebGUI ➔ Agent Station ➔ AI Providers and click Apply.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</DocsLayout>
